    "result_text": "All 64 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate-detection logic to match the spec. Changes across two files:\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- **`identityKey(owner)`** now returns `sha256Hex(normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName))` \u2014 a 64-char lower-case hex digest \u2014 instead of the old plain `telephone|email|householdId` concatenation.\n- Added a self-contained **American Soundex** implementation (`soundex` + `soundexDigit`) so there's no dependency on an undeclared transitive `commons-codec`.\n- **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** (soft match) now triggers when an existing non-deleted owner shares `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode but has a **different** `identityKey` (was: same lastName + postcode + different telephone). Lowest matching id wins for determinism.\n- **Removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block** (`rejectHouseholdDuplicate` call, method, and the `HouseholdDuplicateException` import). Duplicate detection is now solely the identity key. `householdId` is still computed and returned (Cp11/Cp36 rely on it); the email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`) and deleted owners are still ignored.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Updated its `identityKey` to the same SHA-256-over-soundex form so the DTO's `identityKey` field agrees with the controller.\n- Added matching `sha256Hex` and `soundex` helpers (made `private` so MapStruct doesn't mistake them for `String\u2192String` property-mapping methods).\n\nBehavioural results verified by the suite: identical full identities still 409 (Cp03/Cp25/Cp28/Cp52); same lastName+postcode with different telephones are now a soft match rather than a hard 409 (Cp10/Cp35); `identityKey` is a 64-hex string; and no regressions elsewhere.",
